<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32241" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκορέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sweep clean,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς κλίνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					22.12
				</span></i>
			 (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκορίσας</span>):
			metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ᾽κκόρει τὴν Ἑλλάδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					59
				</span></i>
			 ; and (with a play on <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρη</span>)
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ἐξεκόρησέ σε</span>; who
				<i>has robbed</i> you <i>of your daughter?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Th.</u>
				760
			</span></i> : generally, <i>sweep away,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν τῦφον, τὴν κραιπάλην,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.37
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκορηθείης σύ γε</span>”
				<i>clear out! pack off!</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Georg.</u>
					53
				</span></i>
			 : prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκόρει, κόρη,
			κορώνην</span> maiden, <i>drive away</i> the crow—
			the opening of a wedding song—the crow being a prognostic
			of widowhood, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Carm.Pop.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Horap.
				1.8
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
